    "title": "Cheese sold at Whole Foods in several states recalled due to allergy risk of undeclared ingredient - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Mark Richardson ,\n2 days ago Whole Foods Market is recalling Fromagerie Coop de Mean Cabricharme cheese because the product contains egg lysozyme which is not declared on the product label. People who are allergic to eggs or who have a severe sensitivity run the risk of a serious or life-threatening allergic reaction if they consume the product. Read full article",
